# Hook authoring rules

`hooks.json` only wires `record-session` (sessionStart), `block-dangerous`
(beforeShellExecution), and `block-env-read` (beforeReadFile). Do not re-add
conductor hooks (`goal-audit-gate`, `log-trajectory`, `protect-loop-core`,
`verify-gate`). See [0014](../../docs/decisions/0014-pstack-only-no-engineering-loop.md).

## Removed, not wired

`format-and-typecheck` scripts may still sit on disk; they are not in
`hooks.json`. The Stop-hook `verify-gate` scripts are gone (the
`.cursor/skills/verify-gate` skill remains for on-demand gate runs).

**Why verify-gate was not a hook:** it ran `bun run lint && typecheck && test`
across the whole monorepo on every turn — redundant with deliberate gate runs,
and slow enough to false-fail. User confirmation: no marginal safety in an
attended session.

**Why format-and-typecheck stayed unwired:** it read an env var Claude Code never
sets, so it was a silent no-op. Wiring stdin would have reintroduced that
cost on every Write/Edit.

## Hook input arrives as JSON on stdin

Cursor delivers the payload on stdin, not as environment variables. Scripts must
`ConvertFrom-Json` / parse stdin. A hook that only reads `$env:SOMETHING` is a
no-op.

## `.cursor/hooks/*.ps1` must be ASCII-only

Windows PowerShell 5.1 decodes a `.ps1` with no BOM as cp1252, so a non-ASCII
character inside a string literal breaks the script.

## Do not chain `bash || pwsh`

A failing bash script with a missing `pwsh` would hide the real exit code.
`hooks.json` calls each `.ps1` via `powershell -File`. `grep -c '||' .cursor/hooks.json`
returns 0 and must stay 0.
